I am certainly not too good for NetHack. I haven't even ascended. ;)
But even so, I think my lack of ascension at this point stems from a
certain amount of carelessness on my part rather than the difficulty of
the game in general. And don't get me wrong, nethack is very difficult,
but my point is, once you're pretty thoroughly educated (spoiled) in
how the game works, you realize that the pieces are all there. You
always have a luckstone, you always have either a BoH or an AoR. You
always have an AoLS and BoWW, you always have that wand of wishing.

You have a very very good chance of finding any or all off the
following: FooDSM, co-aligned altar, boots of various flavors, helm of
brilliance, gauntlets of power, Wand of Polymorph, etc. Holy water and
full healing can be alchemized, missing armor can be polypiled. Wand of
Wishing pretty much guarantees that you can wish up at least 4 items (1
charge for blessed scoll of charging, plus 3, plus 1 wrested). So right
there, you have 4 chances to get items that you didn't find, and that
doesn't count finding another wand, or wishing on a lamp, a smoky
potion, a throne, or a fountain.

Perhaps my opinion will change once I've had to deal with Rodney and
the Riders, but I just feel like we're guaranteed all this *stuff* and
so NetHack becomes less about ingenuity and more about applying
guaranteed formulas for success.



